<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tubba'</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tubba' was the name by which Arab and Islamic tradition remembered the kings of Himyar in ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. The Qur'an mentions the people of Tubba' as a people destroyed for their sins, and later legend made the Tubba' kings great conquerors who campaigned as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. Many Arab tribes traced their descent through Himyar to Qahtan.</p></div>
